cff-version: 1.2.0
title: hrv_variants
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file, and
  cite the methods papers listed in the README alongside it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: The hrv_variants authors
repository-code: "https://github.com/glig95/heart_rate_variants"
abstract: >-
  Finds amino-acid variants in cardiac ion-channel genes associated with resting
  heart rate across mammals. Three methods are implemented: phylogenetic
  generalized least squares, a clade-sharing test that uses only comparisons made
  within groups of related species, and a gradient-boosted tree model. The
  program has a window, so no code has to be written to use it.
keywords:
  - comparative genomics
  - phylogenetic comparative methods
  - heart rate
  - ion channels
  - mammals
